hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19683","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah from Amr ibn Sharid from his father al-Sharid ibn Suwayd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was sitting thus, having placed my left hand behind my back and leaning upon the fleshy part of my hand. He said: Do you sit the sitting of those upon whom anger fell."
"19684","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us from Abu Salamah from al-Sharid, that his mother bequeathed that they free on her behalf a believing slave. He asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, and said: I have a black Nubian slave-girl, shall I free her on her behalf. He said: Bring her. I called her and she came. He said to her: Who is your Lord. She said: Allah. He said: Who am I. She said: You are the Messenger of Allah. He said: Free her, for she is a believer."
"19685","Waki narrated to us, Wabr ibn Abi Dulaylah, a shaykh of Taif, narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Maymun ibn Musaykah, and he praised him well, from Amr ibn al-Sharid from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Delay by one who can pay makes lawful his honour and his punishment. Waki said: His honour is complaint against him, and his punishment is his imprisonment."
"19686","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Abdullah, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yala ibn Kab al-Thaqafi al-Taifi, narrated to us, he said: I heard Amr ibn al-Sharid narrating from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked me to recite to him from the poetry of Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt, so I recited to him, and whenever I recited a verse to him he said: More, until I recited to him a hundred rhymes, and he said: He almost accepted Islam."
"19687","Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Maysarah informed me from Amr from al-Sharid, that he informed him from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when he found a man lying upon his face with nothing upon his buttocks, he kicked him with his foot and said: This is the most hateful lying to Allah Mighty and Majestic."
"19688","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah informed us from Amr ibn Shuayb from al-Sharid ibn Suwayd al-Thaqafi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbour of the house is more entitled to the house than another."
